# DURABLE REPRO — the `&`-in-an-OWNING-POSITION class, costume 1 of 7:
# a STRUCT-CONSTRUCTOR argument.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C and LLVM): `gg check` is clean, the
# program runs, and the sigil is silently DROPPED — it prints 10, the same as
# the unsigilled spelling. `ggdef` REJECTS: "`&`-alias into an owning position
# is not valid". Both production backends agree on the wrong answer; per Core #8
# that is two bugs, not a wash.
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check`. D10(b) ADDENDUM 3 ratifies aggregate
# construction as an OWNERSHIP BOUNDARY (the field must own), and D31
# full-strict defines `&` as "the callee writes through" — which a constructor,
# having taken ownership, cannot do. A sigil with no meaning at a position is
# not a no-op to be quietly accepted; it is a Core #10 silent drop of user
# syntax.
#
# The `fd` seed is COMPUTED, not a literal, so nothing const-folds.
#
# SIBLINGS — the whole class, each with its own fixture because Core #4 says fix
# the class, not the instance:
#   ..._ctor.gg (this)  ..._push.gg  ..._enum.gg  ..._dict_literal.gg
#   ..._array_literal.gg  ..._tuple_literal.gg  ..._return.gg
# plus the POSITIVE control `sound_amp_named_bind_control.gg` (already rejects
# correctly, must stay rejecting) and the DROP facet
# `security/sound_amp_array_literal_duplicate_drop.gg`.
#
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the `&`-at-a-constructor-position
# entry, widened to the full class.
struct Counter:
    int fd

struct Wrap:
    int held

int seed():
    return 10

void main():
    Counter c = Counter(seed())
    Wrap w = Wrap(&c.fd)
    print(w.held)
